# {{PROJECT_NAME}} Change Record Rules

This file defines how non-trivial changes are recorded.

## Principle

Git records code differences. Change records explain:

- why the change happened
- how the decision was made
- what was verified
- how rollback works
- what data or operational side-effects exist

## File Layout

- index and rules: `{{CHANGE_RECORDS_FILE}}`
- detailed records: `docs/change-records/YYYY-MM-DD-short-topic.md`

## Required Sections Per Record

1. title
2. date
3. executor
4. branch
5. related commit(s)
6. background
7. analysis
8. chosen plan
9. execution
10. verification
11. rollback
12. data side-effects
13. follow-up
14. architecture-boundary check

